Not an upstream patch: this is a Charmed Superset addition, not a backport
of an upstream Superset fix (unlike the 41001/39835 patches alongside it).

Why: `superset mcp run` serves the MCP protocol over streamable-HTTP, which
only answers POST at `/mcp` (confirmed live: GET / -> 404, GET /mcp -> 405,
GET /health -> 404 — there is no HTTP route anywhere in the mcp_service app
that a plain GET can hit). Pebble's `http` check type only ever issues a
GET and expects a 2xx, so `charm.py::_mcp_health_url()`'s
`http://localhost:{port}/health` had nothing to probe: the check stayed
`down` on every attempt, and the mcp application never left
`MaintenanceStatus("Status check: DOWN")` once its auth config allowed it to
start, confirmed via a manually-deployed unit's `pebble checks`/`pebble
logs`.

What it adds: a `/health` route on the same FastMCP ASGI app, registered via
`FastMCP.custom_route()` — the framework's own documented mechanism for
attaching plain HTTP routes alongside the MCP protocol mount (confirmed
present on the exact `fastmcp==3.4.4` pinned in `rock-requirements.txt`).
Returns a bare 200 `PlainTextResponse("OK")`; carries no auth requirement
and no application-level checks (e.g. database connectivity), since
`_metadata_database_status()` on the charm side already gates startup on
the metadata database being reachable and migrated — this route only needs
to prove the ASGI server process itself is alive and serving.

--- a/superset/mcp_service/app.py
+++ b/superset/mcp_service/app.py
@@ -418,6 +418,26 @@ def create_mcp_app(
 # Create default MCP instance for backward compatibility
 mcp = create_mcp_app()

+# Charmed Superset addition: the MCP protocol itself only answers POST at
+# /mcp, so a plain HTTP liveness probe (Pebble's `http` check, a GET
+# expecting 2xx) has nothing to hit. This route gives it one.
+from starlette.requests import Request  # noqa: E402
+from starlette.responses import PlainTextResponse  # noqa: E402
+
+
+@mcp.custom_route("/health", methods=["GET"], include_in_schema=False)
+async def _pebble_health_check(request: Request) -> PlainTextResponse:
+    """Report liveness for Pebble's HTTP check.
+
+    Args:
+        request: The incoming HTTP request.
+
+    Returns:
+        A plain 200 response.
+    """
+    return PlainTextResponse("OK")
+
+
 # Initialize MCP dependency injection BEFORE importing tools/prompts
 # This replaces the abstract @tool and @prompt decorators in superset_core.api.mcp
 # with concrete implementations that can register with the mcp instance
